				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				913,
				3
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Wind): Strip IPC from Electron layer, finalize barrel exports\n\nComplete the IPC de-Effect-ification cleanup. The three Electron layer stacks\n(ElectronBaseLayer, ElectronLiveLayer, ElectronDevLayer) no longer register\nIPCElectronLive — IPC is a plain object imported directly.\n\nRenames barrel exports to the plain-object convention: TauriIPCLive as IPCLive\nand MockIPCLive as IPCMockLive, replacing the old Effect-TS aliases\n(IPCElectronLive, IPCTag as IPC, IPCMockLive, IPCTauriLive). Promotes IPC\nerror classes from export type to export (now concrete Error subclasses).\nSurfaces new IPC helper types (IPCEvent, IPCEventListener, IPCEventStream,\nIPCCleanup) in the main Effect barrel.",
			"SHA": "8c1067c411e40266ff73ea9c737a2187e8c168d6"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T21:42:54Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				913,
				5
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Wind): Finalize IPC De-Effect-ify — clean up barrel, delete Live/Tag, convert Mock\n\nComplete the IPC service migration away from Effect-TS, following the core conversion in 0aeaeb8a that rewrote the errors, interface, and implementation. This commit cleans up the Effect scaffolding that the prior conversion left behind.\n\n**Main barrel** (`Effect/IPC.ts`): Move error-class re-exports from inline definitions to the sub-barrel; replace default-import of Effect-TS Layer with direct implementation imports; add backward-compatibility aliases (`IPCTauriLive`, `IPCMockLive`) using `export { X as Y } from` syntax.\n\n**Deleted files**:\n- `Effect/IPC/Live.ts` — the `Layer.effect(IPCTag, …)` factory; no longer needed since the implementation is a plain object, not an Effect Layer.\n- `Effect/IPC/Tag/IPCTag.ts` — the `Context.GenericTag<IPCService>`; no longer needed since consumers import `TauriIPCLive` directly.\n\n**Mock** (`Effect/IPC/Mock.ts`): Convert from `Layer.succeed(IPCTag, {…})` to a plain `IPCService` object. All methods drop the curried `(_args) => …` Effect signature: `send` returns `void`, `invoke` returns `Promise`, `events` returns an `{ subscribe }` object, `once` takes a callback.\n\n**Sub-barrel** (`Effect/IPC/index.ts`): Remove Tag, Layer, and error-helper (`Create*`) re-exports. Add type exports for the new `IPCEvent`, `IPCEventListener`, `IPCEventStream`, `IPCCleanup` types.\n\n**Impact**: Eliminates the last Effect-TS dependency from Wind's IPC layer. Cuts ~80 lines of Effect boilerplate (Layer, Tag, factory helpers). All imports now come from plain TypeScript modules.",
			"SHA": "fe858d9d20ff1f67eadca05a554d54fc0194c89c"
		}
	],
